04 #edb/ref 17592186301087 13194139534645 true] [17592186301082 1110 #uuid "03c4fb85-a321-5467-af16-32cb80b70300" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301083 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301083 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301083 1111 #uuid "c930386a-5136-50f9-bf20-479eba8d6892" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301084 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301084 1111 #uuid "d7a66c1e-b543-54e9-ad40-3e1a17d51057" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301085 1034 "I only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301085 1111 #uuid "08d85b01-5aec-5012-a7ac-13b39491c69d" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301086 1034 "III only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301086 1111 #uuid "d06a73e0-fd44-541b-9c6e-d6e5a928888b" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301087 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301087 1111 #uuid "75789265-9f31-5dde-aa0a-9bd5faad30f5" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301089 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1089 "q-80331" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1100 "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belong?" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1113 #uuid "b502dfb2-0f40-5bef-86cd-aca89e52845b" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301088 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-\\frac{27}{3}=-9$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-9$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Q,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in R,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only.\"" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301090 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301091 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301092 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301093 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301094 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1041 "selection" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301091 13194139534645 true] [17592186301089 1110 #uuid "2aa147b5-3102-5493-aadb-58120a190f2a" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301090 1034 "$N,Z,Q,R,$ and $C$" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301090 1111 #uuid "5486692f-1eb0-5037-a645-b1d4cfabe7b2" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301091 1034 "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301091 1111 #uuid "23f4b43e-edda-585a-bbc1-30b738dbd4cc" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301092 1034 "$Z$ and $Q$ only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301092 1111 #uuid "61c53909-30e8-5e50-8721-b319debc56d6" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301093 1034 "$Q$ only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301093 1111 #uuid "87b83bef-3ae9-59af-9500-d2d18f9613b9" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301094 1034 "$C$ only" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534645 true] [17592186301094 1111 #uuid "0992376b-0904-55ef-8228-f99f313acf35" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301096 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1089 "q-80332" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1100 "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\pi $ belong?" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1113 #uuid "a1973e12-faf1-5501-b0cf-2ab6d71157b9" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301095 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $\\pi $ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $Z$ nor to $N,$ so we can write\n\n$$\n\\pi \\notin N,\\,\\pi \\notin Z.\n$$\n\n- Also, notice that $\\pi =3.14159\\,…\\,$ can not be written as the ratio of two integers, so it does *not* belong to $Q$ either, and we can write \n\n$$\n\\pi \\notin Q.\n$$\n\n- Every irrational number is both a real number and a complex number. Consequently, $\\pi $ belongs to both $R$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n\\pi \\in R,\\,\\pi \\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ and $C$ only.\"" 13194139534645 true] [17592186301096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301097 13194139534645 true] [17592186301096 1000 #edb/ref 17592